@title Course Portal Single Sign-On
@subtitle How sign-in works for the Kestrel Learning course portal
@author Platform team
@date 2026-10-08

!!! A one-time code **expires after 60 seconds** and **works only once**. A second use, or a use after 60 s, must be rejected.

## Sign-in sequence
diagram sso sequence title="Sign-in"
sso: browser "Browser" user
sso: portal "Course Portal" svc
sso: idp "Identity Provider" svc
sso: tokens "Token Service" svc
sso: dir "User Directory" db
sso: audit "Audit Log" store
sso: browser -> portal : open /courses
sso: portal --> browser : redirect to Identity Provider
sso: browser -> idp : authorization request with PKCE
sso: idp -> dir : verify credentials and groups
sso: dir --> idp : verified, groups returned
sso: idp -> tokens : issue tokens
sso: tokens --> idp : tokens issued
sso: idp --> browser : redirect with one-time code
sso: note browser : code valid 60 s, single use
sso: browser -> portal : one-time code
sso: portal -> tokens : exchange code for tokens
sso: tokens -> audit : record sign-in
sso: portal --> browser : session cookie, 24 hours

## Token lifetimes
data life = token,seconds; One-time code,60; ID token,600; Access token,1800; Refresh token,28800; Session cookie,86400
table = Token,Lifetime; One-time code,**60 seconds, single use**; ID token,10 minutes; Access token,30 minutes; Refresh token,8 hours; Session cookie,24 hours

## Rules
- Staff accounts must pass **MFA**.
- A one-time code can be used **once only**.
- Sign-in events are kept for **400 days**.
